    {
      "id": "overview",
      "title": "Overview",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Brass instruments produce sound by buzzing lips into a cup mouthpiece — air column resonates in tubular metal."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "trumpet",
      "title": "Trumpet",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Three valves lower pitch by semitones. B♭ trumpet most common (transposing — written C sounds B♭). Natural trumpet (no valves) used in Baroque. Jazz, orchestral, and brass band repertoire."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "trombone",
      "title": "Trombone",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Slide changes tube length — no valves. Seven positions. Unique glissando capability. Sacred (Gabrieli) to jazz (J.J. Johnson) to ska."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "french-horn-tuba",
      "title": "French horn, tuba",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Horn: coiled tubing, hand-stopping technique, mellow tone. Tuba: lowest brass, bass foundation in bands."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
